  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Tear 4 Eddie** (1 review): Fowler played a white Fender Strat on it, which the reviewer found unreal and the show's gem [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Never Squeel on a Pusher**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [4]\n- **Springtheme**: with Rev. Bill Fowler [4]\n- **Push tha' Little Daisies**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [4]\n- **If you Could Safe Yourself, You'd Save us All**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Tear 4 Eddie**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 5 archived performances; with Rev. Bill Fowler [4]\n- **Polka Dot Tail**: back after 44 archived shows (561 days); with Rev. Bil Fowler [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **Ween2002-03-21** (recommended): source not stated; 32 songs; 166 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]\n- **ween2002-03-21.mk4v.sxm2.sbm1.d100**: source not stated; 1 songs; 155 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Guests: Rev. Bil Fowler, Rev. Bill Fowler [1]\n- Venue is an old hotel with a bar resembling a wild west saloon; Chimay was available [3]\n- Underage kid was turned away at the door; the room was packed, hot and electric [3]",
